{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ndef ch(b): return {\\\"field\\\":\\\"scenario\\\",\\\"reference\\\":b+\\\".scenario\\\"}\nexp={\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_node_proposal_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"node-propc-guard\\\",\\\"node-propc-restore\\\",\\\"node-propose-block\\\",\\\"node-propose-doc\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":[{\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"node-propc-restore\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"run\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":343,\\\"end_line\\\":343},\n            {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"node-propose-block\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"stepWithWaitOption\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":514,\\\"end_line\\\":514}],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe the application-facing proposal path of the Node wrapper (Node.Propose) for one wrapped node 2 that is removed from the configuration by leader 1 and then added back by the same leader in the same term, comparing Propose before the removal, after the re-add and with the leader's log index before and after each call.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Two voters {1,2} in one process: node 2 is driven through the Node wrapper (newNodeTestHarness, so Readys are consumed and Advance is called) while node 1 is a bare raft instance driven by the harness's message pump; node 1 is made leader directly and broadcasts its appends.\\\",\n   \\\"Both nodes apply the removal and the re-add through the application path (n1.applyConfChange and the wrapper's ApplyConfChange), and every snapshot of node 2 is taken through its status channel (node.Status), which is executed inside the run loop.\\\",\n   \\\"Propose is called with a 300ms context deadline; a nil proposal channel makes the call return only when that deadline fires.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"StepDownOnRemoval, CheckQuorum and PreVote configurations.\\\",\\\"A leadership-change control: the draft attempted to restore the channel by campaigning node 2, but that attempt is not part of this basis.\\\",\\\"Snapshots and asynchronous storage writes.\\\"]},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Create the wrapped node 2 and a bare node 1 over storages with voters {1,2}; make node 1 leader at term 1 and broadcast its appends; pump messages until node 2 (through its status channel) knows leader 1 and has committed the bootstrap entry; propose through the wrapper and record the outcome; propose the removal of node 2 on node 1, pump, and apply it on both nodes; propose the re-add of node 2 on node 1, pump, and apply it on both nodes; then propose through the wrapper again and record the outcome and the leader's log index around it.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"Node.Propose is the application-facing proposal path: its documentation states that it proposes data to be appended to the log and warns only that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140). A node that the application has added back to the configuration, and that knows the leader of that configuration, must therefore be able to hand a proposal to raft - or report why it cannot - rather than block until the caller's context expires while the group never sees the proposal.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"raft (target): the wrapper's own bookkeeping decides whether the application's proposals reach the group, and the target's comment at node.go:409-411 records that this bookkeeping is unsound.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"s0\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"setup\\\"},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adv\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"propose_before_removal\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[ch(\\\"s0\\\")]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"rem\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"node2_removed\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[ch(\\\"adv\\\")]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"node2_readded\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[ch(\\\"rem\\\")]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"propose_before_removal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"s0\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"proposal_returned_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: while node 2 is a plain member of {1,2} and knows leader 1, Propose returns without error.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"propose_before_removal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"s0\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leader_advanced\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the proposal forwarded by the follower reaches the group - the leader's log index advances.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"node2_removed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adv\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leader_sees_member\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Premise: after the removal is applied on both nodes, the leader's configuration no longer contains node 2.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"node2_readded\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"rem\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leader_sees_member\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Premise: after the re-add is applied on both nodes, the leader's configuration contains node 2 again and node 2 has caught up to the leader's log.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"node2_readded\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"rem\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"known_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Premise: the wrapped node still knows leader 1 in the same term, so the leadership is unchanged across the removal and the re-add.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"propose_after_readd\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"add\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"proposal_returned_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"antecedent\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"known_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Witness: with node 2 a member again and still knowing leader 1, Propose returns only when its context deadline fires (context deadline exceeded after about 300ms).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"propose_after_readd\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"add\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leader_advanced\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Witness: the proposal never reached the group - the leader's log index is unchanged across the call.\\\"}]}\nu={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Request the first execution for the Node-wrapper proposal question now that the harness has been repaired: the wrapped node is driven through its status channel for every snapshot, the bare leader broadcasts its appends (a bare becomeLeader does not), and the observations are the application-facing Propose outcome plus the leader's own log index around each call. The draft run shows the control passing before the removal and the witness blocked after the re-add with the same leader and term; the attempted leadership-change control is not part of this basis and stays a limitation.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":exp}\nopen('update15.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update15.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
